       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and overdose can cause shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg or 10 mg.\n\nThere's also a process issue. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. I can't verify that this order came from one.\n\nWhat I suggest:\n- **If a prescriber intended this order,** they should confirm the dose and enter it themselves, or tell me the corrected dose. Typical dosing is 2.5\u20135 mg once daily to start, up to 10 mg once daily.\n- **If you're relaying a request,** please ask the treating clinician to confirm the drug, dose, and indication.\n\nOnce I have a confirmed dose from the prescriber, I can enter it right away, for example amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily."
